      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): protect ConfigurationManager mutable state with NSLock",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`ConfigurationManager` is an `@unchecked Sendable` process-wide singleton with mutable `configuration` and `credentials` and no lock.\n\nThis PR backs both fields with an `NSLock` via locked getters/setters.\n\n## Failure scenario\n\n1. One task reloads configuration while another reads credentials/providers.\n2. Unsynchronized dictionary mutation can tear or lose updates under concurrency.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nConcurrent lock-backed credential read/write stress (same locking shape as the PR):\n\n```\nFINAL_KEYS=5\nPROOF_OK\n```\n\nAlso: `swift build --target PeekabooAutomation` → complete.\n\n## Scope\n\nStorage synchronization only.",
